Let $P,b\in A_+$ be contractions, and suppose that $[P]\leq K[b]$ for a finite positive integer $K$. If $\tau$ is a lower semicontinuous extended trace with $d_\tau(b)<\infty$, then its restriction to $D=\operatorname{her}(P)$ extends to a bounded positive linear functional satisfying $$\label{model:corner-bound}
 \|\tau|_D\|\leq d_\tau(P)\leq Kd_\tau(b).$$ Consequently, for $y,z\in D_+$, $$\label{model:corner-error}
 |\tau(y)-\tau(z)|
    \leq \|y-z\|K d_\tau(b).$$

Fix $m,N\geq1$, and let $\mathcal T=\{1,\ldots,N\}^m$. For every $t\in\mathcal T$ and $S\subseteq\{1,\ldots,m\}$, there are positive contractions $(P_{S,t,i})_{i\geq1}$ in $A$ with the following properties.*

1.  *For fixed $t,i$, the family $(P_{S,t,i})_S$ is orthogonal; in particular, $\sum_S P_{S,t,i}\leq1$.*

2.  *For every $a\in A$, $\|[P_{S,t,i},a]\|\to0$. If $1\leq j\leq m$ and $j\notin S$, then $$\|P_{S,t,i}^{1/2}x_jP_{S,t,i}^{1/2}\|\longrightarrow0.$$*


3.  *If $j\in S$, then $P_{S,t,i}\in I_j$, and there is a finite positive integer $K_{S,t,i,j}$ such that $$\label{model:finite-rank-bound}
      [P_{S,t,i}]\leq K_{S,t,i,j}[b_j].$$*


4.  *For every $a\in A$, $$\label{model:slicing-approximation}
      \limsup_{i\to\infty}
      \left\|\frac1{N^m}\sum_{t\in\mathcal T}\sum_S
         P_{S,t,i}^{1/2}aP_{S,t,i}^{1/2}-a\right\|
      \leq\frac mN\|a\|.$$

For each $j$ there are nonnegative numbers $\varepsilon_{n,j}\to_\omega0$, independent of the trace, with the following properties. Let $\lambda$ be any lower semicontinuous extended trace on $R$, and let $\tau=\lambda|_A$. If $d_\tau(b)<\infty$, then, for $i=0,1$ and $\eta>0$, $$\label{trace:small-rank}
 d_\lambda((u_{n,i}-\eta)_+)
   \leq\eta^{-1}\varepsilon_{n,j}d_\tau(b).$$ If $\ell_n\leq1/4$, then, with no finiteness assumption, $$\label{trace:large-rank}
 d_\lambda((z_n-\gamma/16)_+)
   \geq(\gamma/16)d_\tau(b).$$

For $i\in\{0,1\}$ and every positive contraction $c\in C_i$, $$\begin{aligned}
 m[(c^{1/2}ec^{1/2})^{(i)}]&\leq[Q_0],
       &&m\in\mathbb N,\label{comm:small-part}\\
 [c^{(i)}]&\leq2[Q_0]
       &&\text{in }W(C).\label{comm:two-common}
\end{aligned}$$
